15:12.265 --> 15:14.191
♪ It's Dominick the donkey ♪

15:14.216 --> 15:16.291
♪ Chingedy ching, hee-haw, hee-haw ♪

15:16.316 --> 15:17.649
♪ The Italian Christmas donkey ♪

15:17.674 --> 15:18.704
♪ La, la, la-la ♪

15:18.729 --> 15:20.130
Ooh, like the movie!

15:20.155 --> 15:22.097
♪ La-la, la, la, la, la, la ♪

15:22.122 --> 15:26.457
♪ La, la, la, la, la,
la-lee, oh, dah! ♪

15:26.482 --> 15:28.228
Again.

15:33.774 --> 15:36.208
Hey, sorry about last night, bro.

15:36.233 --> 15:38.541
- No hard feelings?
- Yes, hard feelings.

15:38.566 --> 15:40.005
I told you, I really liked her.

15:40.030 --> 15:42.617
Yo, relax. We only had awesome sex.

15:42.642 --> 15:44.844
Geez. All right, see you later.

15:44.892 --> 15:47.979
I got to go wash Tara's
lipstick off my ass.

15:49.102 --> 15:50.992
Well, at least I have a side,

15:51.017 --> 15:53.410
you neutral Swiss cowards!

15:53.487 --> 15:55.034
Oh, hey, Stewie, how's it going?

15:55.059 --> 15:58.466
Terrible. Johnny Weir's
making my life a nightmare.

15:58.491 --> 16:00.883
I really thought I had a
shot with Tara Lipinski,

16:00.908 --> 16:02.174
and he ruined it.

16:02.317 --> 16:03.983
I'm sorry to hear that.

16:04.008 --> 16:05.874
You want me to take him out for you?

16:05.899 --> 16:08.315
Really? You'd do that for me?

16:08.340 --> 16:10.971
Of course. I owe you for
getting me that job

16:10.996 --> 16:12.059
with Gloria Allred.

16:15.561 --> 16:18.616
<i>They say if you get a job
doing what you love,</i>

16:18.641 --> 16:22.091
<i>you never work a day in your life.</i>

16:25.600 --> 16:28.488
Now it's clothes, now it's clothes,

16:28.513 --> 16:30.103
now it's clothes.

16:30.128 --> 16:33.168
This is for my brother, you
Tom Hiddleston lookalike!

16:33.193 --> 16:36.027
- You serious, bro?
- Oh, no.

16:36.052 --> 16:38.626
Now you're gonna beat me
up like a Batman fight,

16:38.651 --> 16:40.164
only with gay words.

16:40.790 --> 16:41.790
_

16:41.971 --> 16:42.971
_

16:43.867 --> 16:44.867
_

16:45.433 --> 16:46.433
_

16:47.564 --> 16:48.564
_

16:49.379 --> 16:50.379
_

16:51.440 --> 16:52.600
_

16:56.198 --> 16:59.197
Kids, Brian, I've got some bad news.

16:59.222 --> 17:01.649
Your father has been
kidnapped by North Korea.

17:01.674 --> 17:03.131
We've got to save him.

17:03.156 --> 17:04.498
But my race is this afternoon.

17:04.523 --> 17:06.846
I know, but your father needs us.

17:06.871 --> 17:09.545
I don't care. Where was
he when I needed help?

17:09.570 --> 17:11.180
Where were any of you guys?

17:11.205 --> 17:13.171
<i>This was supposed to be my week.</i>

17:13.196 --> 17:16.662
Down here, it's my time.
It's my time down here!

17:16.777 --> 17:18.822
<i>- Is that from Goonies?
- I think so, yeah.</i>

17:18.847 --> 17:20.300
So you guys can all go.

17:20.325 --> 17:22.358
But I'm staying here,
and I'm competing.

17:22.383 --> 17:23.949
And I'm gonna go inside,
outside, inside, outside.

17:23.974 --> 17:25.590
And I'm gonna get 'em on the run, boys.

17:25.615 --> 17:28.189
And once I get 'em on the run,
I'm gonna keep 'em on the run.

17:28.214 --> 17:30.677
Wow, she knows a lot of
Sean Astin speeches.

17:30.702 --> 17:32.635
Go. You don't care.

17:32.660 --> 17:35.686
The only thing you care about
is nugs, chilling and grindage.

17:35.711 --> 17:39.027
<i>Encino Man. Sean Astin, deep cut.</i>

17:47.355 --> 17:49.288
Me? Oh...

17:49.313 --> 17:51.392
Racers, take your mark.

17:52.541 --> 17:54.519
Go, everyone but her.

18:02.523 --> 18:03.923
Wait, before you kill me,

18:03.948 --> 18:05.481
can you at least give
me an extra bullet

18:05.506 --> 18:07.699
so I can pretend to
catch one in my teeth?

18:10.439 --> 18:14.164
Lacey Chabert!

18:14.189 --> 18:16.143
Meg!

18:19.217 --> 18:22.982
_

18:52.486 --> 18:54.184
Meg, that was amazing!

18:54.209 --> 18:55.605
But how we gonna get out of here?

18:55.630 --> 18:58.226
- We're surrounded.
- There's only one way.

18:58.251 --> 19:00.412
An impossible video game escape.

19:00.437 --> 19:02.315
<i>Ooh, can it be GoldenEye?</i>

19:02.340 --> 19:03.929
- Sure.
- Yes!

19:05.028 --> 19:10.006
_

19:10.078 --> 19:13.316
<i>Bond. James Bond.</i>

19:16.231 --> 19:19.085
<i>Don't worry, Meg, it's less
sad because they don't bleed.</i>

19:20.930 --> 19:23.008
<i>Oh, don't shoot this guy.
He was nice to me.</i>

19:23.033 --> 19:25.286
<i>Aw, never mind.</i>

19:25.947 --> 19:28.146
<i>These guys are terrible shots.</i>

19:29.597 --> 19:32.865
<i>I love this almost James Bond music.</i>

19:32.890 --> 19:36.431
<i>Meg, this is what 1997 looked like.</i>

19:36.456 --> 19:39.251
<i>It's my turn next try.
I want to go next.</i>

19:40.155 --> 19:43.567
<i>You think one guy had to
shovel this whole walkway?</i>

19:44.259 --> 19:47.358
<i>Oh, great, more stairs.</i>

19:50.445 --> 19:52.584
<i>This is how you know we're done.</i>

19:59.467 --> 20:01.514
Peter, you're safe!

20:01.539 --> 20:03.538
Yep, and it's all thanks to Meg.

20:03.563 --> 20:05.438
But, Meg, what about your race?

20:05.463 --> 20:07.255
Well, I realized that
it wasn't worth doing

20:07.280 --> 20:09.113
if you guys weren't there with me.

20:09.322 --> 20:11.319
Oh, Meg, we are so sorry

20:11.344 --> 20:12.956
for how we treated you this week.

20:12.981 --> 20:15.348
You may not have won a
gold medal in the games,

20:15.373 --> 20:17.941
but you won one in our hearts.

20:24.325 --> 20:26.288
What do you say, guys,
should we go home?

20:26.313 --> 20:28.050
I don't know, I'm thinking maybe we can

20:28.075 --> 20:29.216
hang out a little bit longer,

20:29.241 --> 20:31.160
see what else Korea has to offer...
Uh-oh.

20:31.185 --> 20:33.469
No! You leave Korea now!

20:33.494 --> 20:38.607
Meet me wherever I land!

20:38.632 --> 20:41.447
<i>Peter landed somewhere in the DMZ,</i>

20:41.472 --> 20:43.713
<i>and was recaptured by North Korea.</i>

20:43.738 --> 20:47.951
<i>Fortunately, tensions caused
by this international incident</i>

20:47.976 --> 20:49.666
<i>were resolved by the steady hand</i>

20:49.691 --> 20:51.249
<i>of Dennis Rodman,</i>

20:51.274 --> 20:53.484
<i>who let Kim Jong-un win</i>

20:53.509 --> 20:55.520
<i>in a one-on-one basketball
game against him,</i>

20:55.545 --> 20:58.098
<i>continuously saying, "Oop, you got me,"</i>

20:58.123 --> 21:00.321
<i>in a way that was just
convincing enough</i>

21:00.346 --> 21:02.209
<i>for Kim to believe.</i>

21:03.424 --> 21:09.354
Thank you for watching "Bob's Burgers " on
www.FOX-fan.tv